A||N||1||Link||The dreaded broken exhaust bolts!!!||||11||
Z||000000||Link||06-20-2000||09:07 PM||||Hi all! I am in a bit of a fix. I had to remove my exhaust manifold on the rear.(2.8 86 GT) I found 1 broken on the lower #5 cylinder and one broke on the upper #1. I thought no problem. Yeah!, none if I could get my hands on a snake drill.<BR> What I would like to do is pick your brains for some suggestions on how to remove the broken studs. This old man's brain is in neutral and really could use some imput. Maybe it will jar the old brain in a forward gear.<BR>Thanks all!||||reg||11
Z||000001||Blaster||06-21-2000||03:09 AM||||Broken Manifold bolts suck. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Anywayz... when I was rebuilding my 2.8 I had a couple break also.. just for future, in case you didn't, try soaking them for a couple days with nut breaker before you try to take them off.  Two ways I know of getting them out is drill and tap and Heli Coil... I sent mine off to a shop to have them shaved and they did it there.. I believe it was heli coiled..<BR>Hope it was some help.. ||||reg||1
